  "caveats": [
    "The frozen rank-1 test is undefined here, not failed: zero ligands carry two pair columns, so there is no shared ligand profile to factorise. The transfer block below is a strictly harder substitute (ligand AND pair both unseen).",
    "The bridge has one parameter and one usable training pair, so alpha is a ratio of descriptor differences, not a fitted coefficient. It cannot be validated inside the training side.",
    "Per-ligand Delta averages over cell lines without weighting; a ligand measured in one cell line and one measured in ten contribute equally.",
    "n_groups here is 347 for Ru-Os vs 354 in the UP-10 audit: this script additionally drops rows with a missing cell_line_key, because the delta key needs one.",
    "pauling_en cannot bridge Ru-Os at all (Ru, Os and Ir all carry 2.20), so the scale is 0.0 and the bridged arm collapses onto the zero arm. ie1_kj is the only descriptor whose sign differs between the two supported pairs.",
    "Ridge on 2048 ECFP4 bits with ~100 training ligands is a high-variance estimator; alpha is chosen on the training pair only, never on the test pair."
  ]
